## Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)

#### Is the maintenance fee optional?
For a perpetual license, maintenance is optional after purchase but highly recommended. Because Udud is under active development, a maintenance subscription ensures you always have access to new engine capabilities and performance improvements. If you choose the quarterly term license, maintenance and support are completely integrated into the single quarterly fee.

#### Do you sell through third-party software resellers?
Yes. We regularly coordinate with corporate software resellers worldwide. Have your preferred procurement partner contact our sales email with your project requirements to initiate the corporate onboarding process.

#### What if our company grows into a higher tier later?
Your pricing structure is locked at the moment of contract execution. If your employee count or annual revenue increases later, your annual renewal and quarterly term rates remain exactly the same as long as your license remains active.

#### Our engineering team is small, but our parent company is an international enterprise. Do we qualify for the startup rate?
No. License tiers are calculated based on the total size of the entire global corporate entity. Larger organizations possess significantly larger market infrastructure to leverage value from the software, and they generally require higher compliance, legal review, and support overhead on our side.
